2026-10-26T13:58:01.1029298Z [0m[1m[38;5;9merror[vulnerability][0m[1m: Non-constant-time mask generation and `u128` comparisons[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1030081Z     [0m[36m┌─[0m /github/workspace/codex-rs/Cargo.lock:399:1
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1030721Z     [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1031314Z [0m[36m399[0m [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31mctutils 0.4.2 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1032292Z     [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m [0m[31msecurity vulnerability detected[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1032885Z     [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1033250Z     [0m[36m├[0m ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0385
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1033805Z     [0m[36m├[0m Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0385
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1034337Z     [0m[36m├[0m ## Summary
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1034640Z       
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1035053Z       The `ctutils::Choice` type has mask generation functions for each unsigned
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1035630Z       integer size (`u8`, `u16`, `u32`, `u64`, `u128`). These are `const fn` and
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1036120Z       therefore can't reuse the `asm!`-backed mask generation in the `cmov` crate
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1036614Z       that's otherwise used to ensure constant-time.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1036961Z       
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1037301Z       In releases prior to v0.4.4, the generated code from these functions could
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1037829Z       include a branch on commonly used platforms. This has been corrected in this
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1038350Z       release and now verified on several platforms using BINSEC.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1038700Z       
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1039921Z       Additionally, `u128` comparison operations provided via `ctutils::Choice` and
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1040769Z       intended to work in constant-time were generating branches on 32-bit targets.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1041491Z       This has been resolved via a special case implementation of these functions
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1042045Z       for such targets.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1042434Z       
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1042775Z       ## Impact
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1043139Z       
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1043678Z       Branch instructions on secret values can potentially leak such values via
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1044631Z       covert channels. This can enable attackers to potentially recover such secrets.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1045334Z       
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1045682Z       ## Resolution
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1046074Z       
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1046666Z       This has been resolved by calling `Choice::to_u8()` when generating the mask,
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1047536Z       which in turn uses `black_box` as an optimization barrier. Verification that
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1048434Z       this resulted in the desired change in the generated assembly across a variety
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1049374Z       of target CPU architectures was performed by BINSEC, which now runs
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1050099Z       automatically in CI using `cargo checkct`.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1051318Z     [0m[36m├[0m Announcement: https://github.com/RustCrypto/utils/pull/1569
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1052721Z     [0m[36m├[0m Solution: Upgrade to >=0.4.4 (try `cargo update -p ctutils`)
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1053203Z 
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1053964Z [0m[1m[38;5;9merror[vulnerability][0m[1m: Data from an abandoned stream leaks into the next stream on a reused context[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1055071Z      [0m[36m┌─[0m /github/workspace/codex-rs/Cargo.lock:1364:1
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1055696Z      [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1056644Z [0m[36m1364[0m [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31mzstd 0.13.3 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1058071Z      [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m [0m[31msecurity vulnerability detected[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1059011Z      [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1059747Z      [0m[36m├[0m ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0391
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1060762Z      [0m[36m├[0m Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0391
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1061837Z      [0m[36m├[0m The `with_context` constructors of the stream encoders and decoders used the
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1062850Z        borrowed context as it was. When a stream was abandoned on a context, for
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1063777Z        example an encoder dropped before `finish()` after an error, whatever it
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1064657Z        left there was carried into the next stream: the input buffered by the
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1065497Z        previous encoder (up to 128 KiB, or all of it with `zstdmt`) became the
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1066305Z        start of the next frame, and a decoder returned undelivered output of the
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1066835Z        previous stream.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1067117Z        
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1067457Z        An application reusing one context for data that must stay separate, such
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1068004Z        as different users' requests, could disclose one user's plaintext to
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1068501Z        another. Whoever supplies the data can cause the abandonment with invalid
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1068936Z        input.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1069192Z        
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1069514Z        The flaw was corrected by resetting the context's session in
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1069918Z        `with_context`.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1070862Z      [0m[36m├[0m Announcement: https://github.com/gyscos/zstd-rs/commit/74ace2dcdca62a2ce0f034895d6079458311e003
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1071594Z      [0m[36m├[0m Solution: Upgrade to >=0.14.3 (try `cargo update -p zstd`)
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1071921Z 
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1072916Z [0m[1m[38;5;9merror[vulnerability][0m[1m: `Seekable::decompress` sets a `Vec` length beyond its capacity for offsets past the end[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1073662Z      [0m[36m┌─[0m /github/workspace/codex-rs/Cargo.lock:1366:1
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1074082Z      [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1074691Z [0m[36m1366[0m [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31mzstd-safe 7.2.4 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1075637Z      [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m [0m[31msecurity vulnerability detected[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1076239Z      [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1076558Z      [0m[36m├[0m ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0398
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1077049Z      [0m[36m├[0m Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0398
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1077675Z      [0m[36m├[0m `ZSTD_seekable_decompress` shortens the requested length to the end of the
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1078297Z        data without checking that the offset is before it. For an offset past the
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1078894Z        end, it returns a wrapped-around length without writing anything, and
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1079386Z        `Seekable::decompress` passed that length to `Vec::set_len`.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1079743Z        
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1080091Z        With the `seekable` feature, whoever supplies the archive, or chooses the
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1080771Z        offset, can leave the caller's `Vec<u8>` with a length far beyond its
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1081551Z        capacity. Reading it then discloses neighbouring heap memory, and appending
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1082174Z        to it corrupts memory. Offsets near `u64::MAX` can also hang the call.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1082601Z        
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1083005Z        The flaw was corrected by clamping requests to the end of the data, and by
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1083567Z        checking every count reported by the C library against the buffer capacity.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1084405Z      [0m[36m├[0m Announcement: https://github.com/gyscos/zstd-rs/commit/80506be743fae2ed0c2fe8b21c374c6a2eab0be7
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1085142Z      [0m[36m├[0m Solution: Upgrade to >=8.2.0 (try `cargo update -p zstd-safe`)
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1085419Z 
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1086024Z [0m[1m[38;5;9merror[vulnerability][0m[1m: Uninitialized memory exposed when streaming decompression of a legacy frame fails[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1086799Z      [0m[36m┌─[0m /github/workspace/codex-rs/Cargo.lock:1366:1
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1087214Z      [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1087805Z [0m[36m1366[0m [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31mzstd-safe 7.2.4 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1088740Z      [0m[36m│[0m [0m[31m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[0m [0m[31msecurity vulnerability detected[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1089327Z      [0m[36m│[0m
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1089723Z      [0m[36m├[0m ID: RUSTSEC-2026-0403
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1090527Z      [0m[36m├[0m Advisory: https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0403
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1091348Z      [0m[36m├[0m When decompression fails inside a legacy (zstd v0.4 to v0.7) frame, the
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1092148Z        bundled zstd library reports the output buffer as fully written although
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1093059Z        nothing was written. `DCtx::decompress_stream` committed that position even
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1093869Z        on error, and for a `Vec<u8>` destination this extended the vector's length
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1094587Z        over uninitialized memory.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1095004Z        
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1095417Z        Legacy support is enabled by default. A 5- or 6-byte corrupt legacy frame is
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1095961Z        enough: through `zstd::stream::write::Decoder`, up to 32 KiB of stale heap
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1096487Z        memory is then passed to the wrapped writer on the next `write()` or
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1097027Z        `flush()`, or when an `auto_flush()`/`on_flush()` decoder is dropped. Whether
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1097595Z        this reaches an attacker depends on where the application sends the
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1098173Z        decompressed output. `zstd::stream::read::Decoder`, `zstd::decode_all` and
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1098598Z        the bulk API are not affected.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1098946Z        
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1099473Z        Before zstd-safe 4.0.0, output buffers could only be initialized slices.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1100605Z        The zstd crate's own writer had the same flaw from 0.4.22 to 0.7.x, which is
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1101241Z        covered by a separate advisory.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1101633Z        
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1102100Z        The flaw was corrected by only committing the buffer positions of a
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1102608Z        successful call.
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1103350Z      [0m[36m├[0m Announcement: https://github.com/gyscos/zstd-rs/commit/006e1d1ad1eeaf6b5d4c28329e70217adabcec43
2026-10-26T13:58:01.1104093Z      [0m[36m├[0m Solution: Upgrade to >=8.2.0 (try `cargo update -p zstd-safe`)
